TRS-80 Model I
Two ALTCPM variants of CP/M 1.4 esisted, Lifefoat and FMG (v1.4 and 1.5)

This is sample procedure to use CPMTOOLS to create a bootable disk image with your own files
(an MS-DOS emulator is required to run bin2imd)

    copy cpm14_empty_body.raw cpm14_body.raw /y
    \cpmtools\cpmcp -f trs1 cpm14_body.raw files\*.* 0:
    copy /B cpm.sys+cpm14_body.raw cpm14.raw /y
    msdos bin2imd cpm14.raw cpm14.imd cpm14.b2i

.. the FMG (fmg_boot.raw) or the Lifeboat (cpm14_boot.raw) core can be copied to CPM.SYS

--------------------------------

CPMTOOLS DISKDEFS:

# TRS80 Model I (ripped header)
diskdef trs1
  seclen 128
  tracks 35
  sectrk 18
  blocksize 1024
  maxdir 64
  skew 4
  boottrk 0
  os 2.2
end

--------------------------------

CPM14.B2I

0  N=35  DM=2  SS=256 SM=0-9 /1
3  DM=2 SS=128 SM=1-18 /1

--------------------------------

